{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-6696",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n- a function is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x$\n\n- a function is odd if $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x$\n\nComputing $f(-x)$ for the given function and comparing it to $f(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\sqrt{20+(-x)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)\\ne f(x),$ the function is not even. \n\nLastly, we compute $-f(x)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-f(x) & =-[\\sqrt{20+x}\\,] \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{20+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)\\ne -f(x)$, the function is not odd. \n\nTherefore, the function is neither even nor odd.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
